  "id": "COMPOUND:11699 - PROTEIN:3787",
  "verbalization": "Anethole trithione appears to have a potential relationship with the Tubulin beta-2B chain, as evidenced by multiple pathways where it is identified as a target of a complex compound with a long chain hydroxylic structure. This compound is known to target multiple protein kinases, including Serine/threonine-protein kinase ULK3 and Tyrosine-protein kinase CSK, which are involved in cellular signaling pathways. The shared target of this compound with Tubulin beta-2B chain suggests a possible mechanism of action involving the regulation of these kinases, which in turn could influence the function of Tubulin beta-2B. The scores from the paths indicate a moderate level of confidence in this relationship, with varying degrees of support from different pathways. The evidence suggests that Anethole trithione may interact with the Tubulin beta-2B chain through a complex network of downstream signaling events, potentially affecting cellular processes related to microtubule dynamics. The integration of these findings highlights the importance of considering the broader biological context in which these interactions occur.",
